{"text": "70: Honorable Mayor and Members of the City Council a\nFROM: Thomas J. Mikulecky x\n\nDATE December 27, 1988\n\nSUBJECT: Amending the 1989 Operating Budget Proposal\n\nAlthough the City Council's instruction was to cut $460,000 from\nthe proposed budget, I have assumed that we could go beyond that\nand, in addition to cuts in proposed expenses, propose transfers\nof balances in other fund accounts and propose new revenues (some\npreviously not considered).\n\nThe Council may then consider each of these items individually in\norder to solve the problem currently before you.\n\nA. Possible reductions in expenditures in the corporate fund.\n\n1, Cut the sewer construction reserve for drainage\nwork. When the balance runs out, transfer the\nauthority for such activity to the sanitary\nsewer fund. Sacrificed: no projects in 1989,\nbut an inability to fund beyond that point.\n\nAccount no. 101-152300-522480 $100,000\n2. Reduce the manhole rehabilitation\nprogram, from $37,470, to the average\nannual expenditure of $17,000.\n\nAccount no. 101-152300-523035 $ 20,000\n\nReduce specialized police training\n(non-recruit) from $49,560 to $34,560,\nwhich is near the average annual\nexpenditure, despite the fact that with an\nexpected increase in the rate of retirements,\ntraining will have to increase.\n\nAccount no. 101-142720-520683 $ 15,000\n\n4. Reduce fire education training from $17,000\nto $12,000, which is again closer to 1988\nactual\u2019 expenditures.\n\nAccount no, 101-143400-523834 $ 5,000\n\nTIILBC 008461", "words": [{"text": "70:", "x0": 113, "y0": 102, "x1": 138, "y1": 131, "conf": 62.0}, {"text": "Honorable", "x0": 203, "y0": 111, "x1": 278, "y1": 121, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Mayor", "x0": 288, "y0": 112, "x1": 330, "y1": 123, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "and", "x0": 340, "y0": 111, "x1": 364, "y1": 121, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Members", "x0": 373, "y0": 111, "x1": 431, "y1": 121, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "of", "x0": 441, "y0": 111, "x1": 457, "y1": 121, 